1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:05,123
One security finding is rarely
the end of an investigation.

2
00:00:05,163 --> 00:00:09,529
A weakness in one service can make a test
of a connected service worth running.

3
00:00:09,569 --> 00:00:13,238
But when an agent's session
ends, its context ends with it.

4
00:00:13,329 --> 00:00:17,742
The next investigator inherits
chat logs, not verified facts.

5
00:00:17,802 --> 00:00:21,545
Arcloom keeps reviewed evidence
in a FalkorDB knowledge graph,

6
00:00:21,585 --> 00:00:26,533
so a fresh investigator can see which
next experiment is justified, and why.

7
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:29,862
We begin with a gateway-boundary
report in our synthetic

8
00:00:29,902 --> 00:00:33,259
lab. A report is still only a claim.

9
00:00:33,594 --> 00:00:38,170
An authorized reviewer approves the
registered test before anything executes.

10
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:42,602
The runner records real HTTP
observations: the baseline is

11
00:00:42,642 --> 00:00:46,397
denied, while the seeded
routing context succeeds.

12
00:00:46,437 --> 00:00:51,510
We verify the evidence against its
signed receipt and SHA-256 digest.

13
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,405
A separate review accepts the observation.
Only then does it become a finding.

14
00:00:57,752 --> 00:01:03,272
That accepted finding is stored in FalkorDB
Cloud: our running instance in Mumbai.

15
00:01:03,312 --> 00:01:06,184
This is the actual knowledge
graph behind the demo,

16
00:01:06,224 --> 00:01:09,909
returned by a read-only
query against that database.

17
00:01:09,949 --> 00:01:15,407
Findings enable capabilities. Tests
require capabilities, and target assets.

18
00:01:15,469 --> 00:01:18,527
The gateway finding enables
internal route access,

19
00:01:18,567 --> 00:01:21,599
exactly what the invoice test requires.

20
00:01:21,914 --> 00:01:25,171
A test is eligible only when
every capability it requires has

21
00:01:25,211 --> 00:01:29,276
current, confirmed support.
The chain test needs two.

22
00:01:30,779 --> 00:01:33,303
A fresh investigator starts
in a separate command-line

23
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:36,537
process, with zero previous messages.

24
00:01:36,877 --> 00:01:41,377
It reads only what FalkorDB returns:
the invoice test requires internal

25
00:01:41,417 --> 00:01:45,044
route access, and the confirmed
gateway finding supplies it.

26
00:01:45,084 --> 00:01:49,763
A model can help choose a candidate, but
it cannot grant permission to run it.

27
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:54,571
Once approved, the invoice test
reproduces a separate tenant-ownership

28
00:01:54,611 --> 00:01:58,630
weakness: one tenant reads
another tenant's invoice.

29
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:01,737
After review, it supplies a second capability.

30
00:02:02,054 --> 00:02:07,094
A second fresh process can now propose the
chain, because both prerequisites exist.

31
00:02:07,288 --> 00:02:11,461
The runner executes the chain under
one synthetic identity and revision.

32
00:02:11,501 --> 00:02:14,433
The graph explains why the
test is worth attempting.

33
00:02:14,473 --> 00:02:18,526
The observations and the review
establish what actually happened.

34
00:02:20,778 --> 00:02:24,193
Useful memory also includes
failure and uncertainty.

35
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:28,867
The export service denies the request,
so that issue is not reproduced.

36
00:02:28,907 --> 00:02:31,628
The unavailable audit service
produces an inconclusive

37
00:02:31,668 --> 00:02:34,387
result. Neither becomes a finding.

38
00:02:34,606 --> 00:02:37,780
Both outcomes stay in memory,
so the next investigator

39
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,736
does not propose the same
attempted work again.

40
00:02:41,856 --> 00:02:44,730
The handoff is inspectable: verified receipts,

41
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:49,172
current support paths, blocked
reasons and negative observations.

42
00:02:49,788 --> 00:02:54,506
Its canonical JSON export
carries a SHA-256 digest.

43
00:02:54,546 --> 00:02:59,371
External agents can read the same memory
through three authenticated MCP tools:

44
00:02:59,411 --> 00:03:04,001
the handoff, the investigation
list, and a single investigation.

45
00:03:04,041 --> 00:03:07,426
These tools are read-only.
Reading memory creates no agent,

46
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:10,939
calls no model, and authorizes no execution.

47
00:03:12,562 --> 00:03:16,969
Evidence can change. Withdrawal analysis
shows which tests would lose support if a

48
00:03:17,009 --> 00:03:21,741
finding were withdrawn, counting any
independent evidence that still holds.

49
00:03:21,781 --> 00:03:25,294
After a deployment moves to
revision r2, old findings remain

50
00:03:25,334 --> 00:03:29,053
in history, but cannot
silently justify new work.

51
00:03:29,093 --> 00:03:32,137
Explicit revalidation
records the new behavior:

52
00:03:32,309 --> 00:03:35,402
the patched gateway now
rejects the routing context.

53
00:03:35,442 --> 00:03:37,735
A blocked gateway can stop this chain.

54
00:03:37,775 --> 00:03:41,167
It does not prove every
downstream service is secure.

55
00:03:42,026 --> 00:03:45,643
Arcloom combines FalkorDB, a
durable investigation journal,

56
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:49,054
signed evidence and a scoped HTTP runner.

57
00:03:49,094 --> 00:03:52,463
Separate live checks validated
ChatGPT Luna and Gemini;

58
00:03:52,635 --> 00:03:56,085
this repeatable demo uses
deterministic selection.

59
00:03:56,369 --> 00:04:00,006
One discovery becomes a justified
next experiment, with evidence that

60
00:04:00,046 --> 00:04:03,521
survives the handoff, and knows
when its support has expired.
